data/
# ⛔⛔ ANCHORED TO contracts/, AND THAT IS NOT TIDINESS. Written bare as `lib/` this rule matched
# EVERY directory named lib at any depth — including `web/src/lib/`, which is 23 files: every chain
# read, the router, the wallet, the claims logic and the launch gate. The public repo shipped
# `App.tsx` importing `./lib/router.ts` with no lib directory beside it, so github.com/sharepons/share
# could not build. Found 4 Sep 2026 by fetching the paths from GitHub, not by reading this file.
# ⚠ The publish audit looked for secrets LEAKING OUT and could not see code FAILING to go out.
# What it is actually for: Foundry's dependency checkout, which is a submodule tree.
contracts/lib/

# Secrets that are templates today and live keys later. ⛔ None of these match the `.env` rule
# above: `.env` matches only a file named exactly that, so `oauth.env` and the pre-deploy backups
# were tracked. They are empty right now, which is exactly why this is cheap to fix.
oauth.env
*.bak-predeploy
.signer.key

# ── ⛔⛔ NEVER PUBLIC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC. These three are internal and each was verified to contain something that
# must not leave the box — see the audit in HANDOFF.md.
#
#   HANDOFF.md            the gate access code, the server IP, and an operational runbook that
#                         catalogues what is weak and where. Useful to us, a map to anyone else.
#   Caddyfile.share       the live gate access code, in the cookie regex. Publishing it opens the
#                         site. ⭐ A redacted copy IS public at deploy/Caddyfile.example.
#   docs/oauth-setup.md   notes a credential exposure affecting SIBLING projects by name.
#
# ⚠ Adding a file here does NOT remove it from history if it was ever committed. Check with
#   `git log --all --oneline -- <path>` before assuming a leak was never published.
HANDOFF.md
Caddyfile.share
docs/oauth-setup.md
